WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.310
The weather client now retries
temporary failures on its own.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.578
When the API is busy,

00:00:07.578 --> 00:00:11.840
forecasts fail with 429,
503 or a network error.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.734
Callers retry by hand.

00:00:14.084 --> 00:00:17.086
The task: retry those failures with

00:00:17.086 --> 00:00:19.587
exponential backoff,
and respect Retry-After.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:23.003
The retry loop lives in a new helper,

00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:25.519
withRetry, so other
calls can use it later.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:28.356
getForecast sends every
request through it,

00:00:28.356 --> 00:00:31.257
and loadConfig reads
three new retry settings.

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:34.475
withRetry fills in defaults
from DEFAULT_RETRY,

00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:37.179
then runs the operation in a loop.

00:00:37.529 --> 00:00:39.600
On a final error, or after the

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.671
last allowed retry, it throws the error.

00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:47.278
Otherwise it waits: afterMs if the
decision has one, or else backoffDelay.

00:00:48.278 --> 00:00:51.079
The defaults: three retries,
a 250 millisecond

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:53.879
base delay and a four second cap.

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:59.202
isRetryableStatus
accepts only 429 and 5xx.

00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:03.697
backoffDelay picks a random wait
below a limit that doubles each time.

00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:05.078
That is full jitter.

00:01:05.978 --> 00:01:11.433
retryDecision retries a
WeatherError only for 429 and 5xx.

00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:14.463
A 404 fails at once.

00:01:14.813 --> 00:01:16.979
A TypeError means fetch got no response,

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:19.455
so it is retried as a network error.

00:01:19.805 --> 00:01:24.157
retryAfterMs reads Retry-After,
in seconds or as a date.

00:01:24.157 --> 00:01:26.574
That wait replaces the backoff.

00:01:27.474 --> 00:01:30.338
Before, the first failure went
straight back to the caller.

00:01:30.688 --> 00:01:34.345
Now, in the first new test,
no response means a

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:37.636
backoff wait, and a 503
waits as Retry-After says.

00:01:37.986 --> 00:01:40.039
The third attempt returns the forecast.

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:42.732
The timeout applies per attempt,

00:01:42.732 --> 00:01:45.440
so the worst case grows with every retry.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:50.360
A long Retry-After is used as sent,
without the maxDelayMs cap.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.330
Timeouts are not retried,
but any TypeError is,

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.968
even one from a bug.

00:01:55.318 --> 00:01:59.199
And WeatherError and WeatherConfig
changed shape, so check the callers.

00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:03.301
Temporary failures now
retry with jittered backoff.

00:02:03.301 --> 00:02:05.959
Other 4xx errors fail at once.

00:02:06.309 --> 00:02:09.481
The coding agent reports
that npm test passed.
